<article class="env-example" id="00YE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00YE">Example <span data-tag="00YE">7.33.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $X_{Zar}$ be the site of Example <a href="/tag/00VJ" data-tag="00VJ">7.6.4</a>. Let $x \in X$ be a point. Consider the functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  u : X_{Zar} \longrightarrow \textit{Sets}, \quad U \mapsto \left\{  \begin{matrix}  \emptyset 

&  \text{if} 

&  x \not\in U 

\\  \{ *\}  

&  \text{if} 

&  x \in U 

\end{matrix} \right.  \]
</div>
  <p> This functor commutes with product and fibred products, and turns coverings into surjective families of maps. Hence we obtain a point $p$ of the site $X_{Zar}$. It is immediately verified that the stalk functor agrees with the stalk at $x$ defined in Sheaves, Section <a href="/tag/0078" data-tag="0078">6.11</a>. </p>
</article>